{"name":"Bonnie’s Bench","hex":"#7c644a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonnie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry; happy.","Beautiful; pretty; attractive; handsome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bonfire; chiefly one several storeys tall and burned to celebrate Eleventh Night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonnie"},{"term":"bench","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long seat with or without a back, found for example in parks and schools.","The seat where the judges sit in court.\n The people who decide on the verdict, collectively; the judiciary."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove a player from play.","To remove someone from a position of responsibility temporarily."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bench"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonnie","blocks":[{"text":"Bonnie is a Scottish feminine given name. It comes from the Scots language word \"bonnie\", or the French bonne (good). That is in turn derived from the Latin word \"bonus\" (good). The name can also be used as a pet form of Bonita."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg/330px-Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonnie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faye Dunaway as Bonnie Parker in the 1967 film Bonnie and Clyde.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File